// Template only. NPDevGenerator materializes this file as settings.gradle in an assembled FinalExec
// app (FinalAppAssembler#materializeRootTemplate -- same substitution-free, byte-for-byte copy
// convention as build.gradle.template).

// deps-and-java/PLAN.md W1.5/Risk 2: without a toolchain resolver, a machine whose only JDK is >17
// (a 21-only machine building an app that stayed at the javaVersion=17 default, or vice versa) fails
// with a bare "No matching toolchains found" instead of Gradle provisioning the missing one itself.
//
// The `plugins {}` block here is NOT a normal method call -- Gradle parses/resolves it specially at
// settings-evaluation time, and it must be the FIRST statement in the file (only buildscript{}/
// pluginManagement{} may precede it; even `rootProject.name = ...` above it is a hard compile
// error, confirmed live -- "only buildscript {}, pluginManagement {} and other plugins {} script
// blocks are allowed before plugins {} blocks"). It also cannot be wrapped in an `if` (a SECOND
// confirmed-live error: "Could not find method plugins()") -- so the opt-out is Gradle's OWN native
// toolchain-provisioning switch, not a conditional plugin registration: this plugin only ever makes
// a network call when NO local JDK already satisfies the requested toolchain, AND ONLY if
// auto-download is enabled -- pass -Dorg.gradle.java.installations.auto-download=false (or set
// org.gradle.java.installations.auto-download=false in gradle.properties) on a machine whose
// network blocks outbound JDK downloads. With auto-download disabled, this degrades to exactly
// today's behavior (Gradle's own unchanged "No matching toolchains found" when nothing local
// matches), never something worse.
plugins {
    // ROUND2_PLAN.md R1c: bumped to the latest release (1.0.0) alongside the Gradle 9.5.1 wrapper
    // bump -- 0.8.0 depended on FoojayToolchainsPlugin, a class Gradle 9 removed.
    id 'org.gradle.toolchains.foojay-resolver-convention' version '1.0.0'
}

rootProject.name = 'FinalExec'
